1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,570
Audit reports say “Fixed”.

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:02,740
Users trust it.

3
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:06,050
Nobody checks the code that's actually deployed.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:06,910
FixCheck does.

5
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:11,330
It read 22 checks of 21 findings marked fixed: 7 fixed,

6
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:17,550
1 not fixed, 6 deployed before the audit, and 1 before its fix existed.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:23,120
This is PoolTogether: one row per finding, its status, and how it was decided.

8
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:24,887
This finding was marked fixed.

9
00:00:24,887 --> 00:00:28,657
On the left, the function the auditors reviewed; on the right,

10
00:00:28,657 --> 00:00:32,087
the one deployed on Ethereum after the fix was merged.

11
00:00:32,087 --> 00:00:33,347
They're identical.

12
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,950
Against the fix commit, the fixed line simply isn't there.

13
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,650
So code alone says: not fixed.

14
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,240
When code can't decide, validators ask a model,

15
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:45,100
but it must quote a line the fix added.

16
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,480
Here it couldn't, so the check is inconclusive and everyone is refunded.

17
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:54,133
To check a finding yourself, pick the report, the finding and the deployed address.

18
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:58,653
Before you pay, the app runs the same checks the contract will.

19
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,880
Then you stake that it isn't fixed.

20
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:04,010
Every validator reads the report, both commits, the verified source,

21
00:01:04,010 --> 00:01:07,380
and when the code and the fix were made.

22
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:10,433
This vault was deployed the day before the audit,

23
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:13,313
so code already says: predates the audit.

24
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:15,097
Code decides everything it can.

25
00:01:15,097 --> 00:01:20,187
The model never decides what counts as evidence, the dates, or the money.

26
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:25,283
The real result: six PoolTogether contracts predate the audit, one vault predates its fix,

27
00:01:25,283 --> 00:01:29,453
and one vault deployed after the fix is not fixed.

28
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,040
Code compares the functions.

29
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:36,050
GenLayer validators only judge the middle cases, and must quote the exact lines.

30
00:01:36,050 --> 00:01:39,150
fixcheck-ledger dot vercel dot app.
